Two classes. StoneGolem overrides greet() and adds a method of its own, smash().
class Golem {
    String greet() { return "hum"; }
}
class StoneGolem extends Golem {
    @Override String greet() { return "GRIND"; }
    void smash() { }
}

Golem g = new StoneGolem();
The variable g has the declared type Golem. The object it refers to has the runtime type StoneGolem. That is legal because a StoneGolem is a Golem.

